  "description": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Drew University is a private liberal arts university founded in 1867 by railroad financier Daniel Drew as Drew Theological Seminary in Madison, New Jersey. Set on a 186-acre wooded campus — including the 80-acre Drew Forest Preserve — just 25 miles from New York City, Drew combines the intimacy of a small residential college with direct access to one of the world's great metropolitan centres.",
      "The university comprises three schools: the College of Liberal Arts offering over 50 undergraduate majors and concentrations, the Caspersen School of Graduate Studies providing master's and doctoral programmes, and the Drew Theological School — one of 13 United Methodist seminaries in the United States. Signature programmes include the BA/MD Dual Degree track, Digital Humanities, and the nycTREC semester immersion experiences placing students inside New York's finance, arts, communications, and policy sectors.",
      "Drew's distinctive TREC (The Real Education Connection) model extends learning across New York City, London, Brussels, Tuscany, and other international locations, offering semester-long immersive programmes where students earn full credit while working alongside professionals. The university is consistently recognised for Social Mobility, ranking 7th nationally (U.S. News & World Report 2026), and is tied for 84th among National Liberal Arts Colleges.",
      "International students are welcomed across all three schools and benefit from dedicated International Student and Scholar Services, English language support, and a strong campus community. Drew's proximity to New York City provides unmatched internship, cultural, and networking opportunities, while the forested campus offers a peaceful residential experience."
    ],
